# Western Digital

> Western Digital Corporation (WD) is a global data storage company headquartered in San Jose, California. Following the 2024 separation from its flash memory business (now operating independently as SanDisk), Western Digital focuses exclusively on hard disk drives (HDD) and HDD-based storage solutions. Key product lines include WD Blue (everyday computing), WD Red / WD Red Plus / WD Red Pro (NAS), WD Purple / WD Purple Pro (surveillance), WD Black (gaming/performance), WD Gold (enterprise), and Ultrastar (data center). WD also sells external drives (My Passport, My Book, Elements, EasyStore), personal cloud/NAS devices (My Cloud), and data center storage platforms (JBOD, EBOF). Western Digital serves consumers, creative professionals, gamers, small businesses, and enterprise data centers worldwide.

